# Caddy ingress — topology level (P19-T02).
#
# This configuration is deliberately thin, and the thinness is the design: it
# answers the question "does the stack have a complete path from the internet
# to the application", which is what the Compose task is responsible for.
#
# P19-T03 owns the hardening that belongs to the ingress itself: TLS Full
# (strict) against the Cloudflare origin, explicit trusted proxies, security
# headers, compression, route and cache behaviour, and upstream health checks.
# P19-T05/T06 own the access logs and the alerting on them. None of that is
# declared here, so that the file this task commits is only the part this task
# can validate.
#
# Two properties are worth stating because they are decisions, not defaults:
#
#   - the certificate is a *file secret* mounted by Compose, not an ACME
#     issuance: the origin accepts traffic only from Cloudflare, so a challenge
#     that needs to be reachable from the internet would turn every renewal into
#     an outage window (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §3);
#   - the upstream is named by service name on the edge network, and the
#     application is the only other member of that network, so the name resolves
#     to one address and a typo cannot silently proxy to something else.

{$COMPOSE_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	tls /run/secrets/origin_certificate /run/secrets/origin_key

	reverse_proxy app:8080
}
